        raise ImproperlyConfigured(
            "AUTH_USER_MODEL refers to model '%s' that has not been installed"
            % settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL
        )
```

It looks up the model class specified by `settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL` from Django's global app registry, raising `ImproperlyConfigured` if the setting is malformed or the model hasn't been installed.
